# Build context hygiene for Phase 8C's images.
#
# The Dockerfiles copy narrow paths, so a leaked line here would only matter if a
# COPY were widened later - which is exactly what this file is for: the context must
# not contain the things that must never reach an image layer, even by accident.
#
# Credentials and local state first: the repo keeps its real values in *.local files,
# and the examples are documentation for humans, not inputs to a build (no COPY line
# reads them).
.git
.gitignore
.env
.env.*
# Both suffix rules stay: the two documented readings of a pattern without a separator
# disagree about subdirectories (Docker's table says root only, the matcher moby ships
# follows .gitignore and matches any depth), and neither reading is relied on. Nothing
# here is tracked under a *.local name, so these two lines can only exclude local state.
*.local
**/*.local
*.env

# Runtime state that belongs to the host, never to an image.
data/
uploads/
bin/
coverage.out

# Build leftovers and scratch files from any round.
*.exe
*.dll
*.test
*.log
*.tmp
*.bak
*.orig
*.pid

# Sealed evidence and verification records: they describe what was proved, and are not
# part of the program.
spec/

# The frontend's own install output and previous build results: the frontend image
# runs `npm ci` and `vite build` inside its own build stage.
web/node_modules/
web/dist/
web/coverage/
web/.vite/
web/test/

# Any directory that came from an earlier project rather than from this build.
GopherAI-v1/
GopherAI-v2/
GopherLearn-v3/
GopherLearn-v3.1/
work/
optimization/
tutorial/
